":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-8","layout":"ComponentLayout-184","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#dcdcdc","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-6","layout":"ComponentLayout-18","role":"container","type":"container"},{"components":[{"components":[{"additions":[{"URL":"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/shaun-walker","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":12,"start":0},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-author-1","layout":"ComponentLayout-212","role":"author","text":"Shaun Walker in Warsaw","textStyle":"_anf-cts-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading6-1","layout":"ComponentLayout-16","role":"heading6","text":"07:35 EST Tuesday, 30 December 2025","textStyle":"_anf-cts-4","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-19","layout":"ComponentLayout-211","role":"container","type":"container"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-7","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","style":"body","type":"container"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-9","layout":"ComponentLayout-18","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#dcdcdc","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-8","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"additions":[{"URL":"https://apple.news/Ai6CzUY9aQbCfLsuSe6j7Uw","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":39,"start":23},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-22","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":233,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-18"},{"range":{"length":233,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-18"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-216","role":"body","text":"Russia alleges Ukraine tried to hit Vladimir Putin’s residence in a mass drone attack on Monday. The foreign minister, Sergei Lavrov, said Russian air defences shot down 91 drones and he called the attack an act of “state terrorism”.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-23","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":251,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":251,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"Ukraine has denied the claim and Volodymyr Zelenskyy accused Lavrov of spreading “typical Russian lies” to try to undermine diplomatic progress between Kyiv and Washington after a bilateral meeting with Donald Trump at Mar-a-Lago in Florida on Sunday.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-24","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":311,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":311,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"The claim, as so much of geopolitics in 2025, seems to have been primarily targeted at an audience of one, Trump, and he seems to have bought it. “It’s one thing to be offensive, because they’re offensive. It’s another thing to attack his house. It’s not the right time to do any of that,” Trump said on Monday.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"additions":[{"URL":"https://apple.news/AEpQfG6fyRbOdrztqkLlkrQ","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":26,"start":26},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-25","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":311,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":311,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"The allegation comes at a delicate diplomatic moment as Trump insists a peace deal between Russia and Ukraine is “95% done”. Zelenskyy is desperately trying to keep the US president onside while Russia has persuaded Trump it is ready for negotiations but appears unwilling to give up on its maximalist war aims.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-10","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-9","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-1","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":34,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":34,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"What evidence has Moscow provided?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"components":[{"components":[{"accessibilityCaption":"Headlines US newsletter","identifier":"_anf-image-1","imageIdentifier":"caf48e021cacd7450da4ed92021bb33a","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"image","type":"image"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-20","layout":"ComponentLayout-16","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"},{"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-image-2","imageIdentifier":"f2787ab648a691cb0dbba23d32051b5c","layout":"ComponentLayout-225","role":"image","type":"image"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-26","layout":"ComponentLayout-224","role":"container","type":"container"},{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-35","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":21,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-16"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-223","role":"body","text":"Free daily newsletter","textStyle":"_anf-moved-5","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-27","layout":"ComponentLayout-226","role":"container","type":"container"}],"contentDisplay":{"type":"horizontal_stack"},"identifier":"_anf-container-23","layout":"ComponentLayout-223","role":"container","type":"container"},{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-1","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":24,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"heading3","text":"Sign up for Headlines US","textStyle":"_anf-moved-6","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-24","layout":"ComponentLayout-228","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"},{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-36","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":90,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-18"}],"layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"body","text":"Start the day with a digest of the morning's main US headlines sent directly to your inbox","textStyle":"_anf-moved-7","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-25","layout":"ComponentLayout-228","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-21","layout":"ComponentLayout-222","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"},{"components":[{"action":{"URL":"https://www.theguardian.com/info/2015/dec/08/daily-email-us?CMP=oth_b-aplnews_d-1","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"type":"link"},"identifier":"_anf-link_button-1","layout":"ComponentLayout-231","role":"link_button","style":"_anf-cs-4","text":"Sign up","textStyle":"_anf-cts-5","type":"button"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-22","layout":"ComponentLayout-230","role":"container","type":"container"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-10","layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-1","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-26","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":326,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":326,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"Absolutely none, and on Tuesday Putin’s spokesperson, Dmitry Peskov, said there would be none forthcoming. “I don’t think there should be any evidence if such a massive drone attack is being carried out, which, thanks to the well-coordinated work of the air defence system, was shot down,” he told journalists in a phone call.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-11","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-11","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-2","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":22,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":22,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"Can Moscow be trusted?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-27","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":467,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":467,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"In a word, no. The Kremlin and the defence ministry often make fantastical claims about the war in Ukraine. Moscow still insists it never targets civilians in its drone and missile raids on Ukraine, despite regular evidence to the contrary. Russian authorities also have a long history of fictitious stories about Ukraine, stretching back to the 2014 annexation of Crimea when Putin claimed the Russian special forces annexing the peninsula were in fact local people.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-12","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-12","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-3","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":57,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":57,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"Does that mean the drone attack definitely didn’t happen?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"additions":[{"URL":"https://apple.news/A0Sw6HAvvRZarqqsaPIxX0g","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":34,"start":113},"type":"link"},{"URL":"https://apple.news/A7V7RNLviR427AHErYK1vaQ","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":44,"start":276},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-28","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":538,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":538,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"It’s hard to say for sure. Ukraine certainly has a history of carrying out strikes deep inside Russia, including assassinations of military figures, drone attacks on oil refineries and, most spectacularly, Operation Spiderweb, in which camouflaged drones launched from trucks destroyed numerous Russian strategic bombers deep inside Russia. Certainly, Putin’s residence would be seen by Ukrainian planners as a legitimate and tempting target. Making the move just at a key point in negotiations with Trump would be an odd choice, however.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-13","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-13","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-4","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":39,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":39,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"If it’s a false claim, what’s the goal?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-29","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":344,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":344,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"There are a couple of possibilities. Zelenskyy has claimed the accusation is a cover story to allow Moscow to strike government buildings in Kyiv, especially as Lavrov has said “retaliatory targets” have already been selected. But as the last four years show, Moscow does not really require cover stories to hit all kinds of targets in Ukraine.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-30","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":478,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":478,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"A more likely scenario would be that Putin, well aware of the theory that Trump is often swayed by the last person he spoke with, was wary of Zelenskyy’s in-person visit to Mar-a-Lago and what might be achieved in the talks. By accusing the Ukrainians of escalation, both publicly and to Trump on the phone, Putin may have been hoping to change the calculus in the US president’s head one more time and stave off any decisions the Kremlin would consider overly friendly to Kyiv.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-14","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-14","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-5","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":17,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":17,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"Did Trump buy it?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-31","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":369,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":369,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"The early indications are Trump believed the claim and was angered by Ukraine’s supposed actions. When a reporter suggested the claim could have been fabricated, Trump appeared to be considering the possibility for the first time. “You’re saying maybe the attack didn’t take place? That’s possible too I guess. But President Putin told me this morning it did,” he said.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-32","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":197,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":197,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"The CIA could presumably give Trump a decent analysis on whether or not it believes the claim is true, but reports suggest the president often ignores the findings of his own intelligence agencies.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"stroke":{"color":"#333333","style":"solid","width":"1.0pt"}}],"identifier":"_anf-divider-15","layout":"ComponentLayout-218","role":"divider","stroke":{"color":"#8b0000","style":"solid","width":"4.0pt"},"type":"line"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-15","layout":"ComponentLayout-1","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-6","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":38,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"},{"range":{"length":38,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-14"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-219","role":"heading2","text":"Does anyone else believe the Russians?","textStyle":"_anf-moved-10","type":"text"},{"additions":[{"URL":"https://x.com/narendramodi/status/2005899780795535587","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":5,"start":169},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-33","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":370,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":370,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"In European capitals the claims have been met with huge scepticism, but elsewhere there are signs that the accusation has landed. India’s prime minister, Narendra Modi, wrote on X in English and Russian that he was “deeply concerned” by the reports. “We urge all concerned to remain focused on these efforts and to avoid any actions that could undermine them,” he added.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-34","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":349,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"},{"range":{"length":349,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-10"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"Ukraine’s foreign minister, Andrii Sybiha, wrote on X on Tuesday: “We were disappointed and concerned to see the statements by Emirati, Indian and Pakistani sides expressing their concerns regarding the attack that never happened.” He said none of the three issued a statement when a Russian missile hit a Ukrainian government building in September.","textStyle":"_anf-moved-3","type":"text"},{"allowAutoplacedAds":false,"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"anchor":{"originAnchorPosition":"top","targetAnchorPosition":"top"},"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"hidden":true}],"hidden":false,"identifier":"_anf-logo-1","imageIdentifier":"a7ca38bc2602f83f638127dffb2a88d4","layout":"ComponentLayout-250","role":"logo","type":"image"},{"anchor":{"originAnchorPosition":"top","targetAnchorPosition":"top"},"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"hidden":false}],"hidden":true,"identifier":"_anf-logo-2","imageIdentifier":"eb5cb46005dc15c3c921417a05fef65b","layout":"ComponentLayout-250","role":"logo","type":"image"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-30","layout":"ComponentLayout-249","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"},{"components":[{"accessibilityCaption":"Help us reach our $2,000,000 goal","conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minColumns":5,"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"light"}],"hidden":false}],"hidden":true,"identifier":"_anf-figure-1","imageIdentifier":"e120f6bcc2ba5c1ddab2294c697ec069","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"figure","type":"scalable_image"},{"accessibilityCaption":"Help us reach our $2,000,000 goal","conditional":[{"conditions":[{"maxColumns":4,"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"light"}],"hidden":false}],"hidden":true,"identifier":"_anf-figure-2","imageIdentifier":"eedf774bdf4abcd93506fedb5e9b53bc","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"figure","type":"scalable_image"},{"accessibilityCaption":"Help us reach our $2,000,000 goal","conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minColumns":5,"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"hidden":false}],"hidden":true,"identifier":"_anf-figure-3","imageIdentifier":"f3bc092e52fe364925b08e1e1baf33b0","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"figure","type":"scalable_image"},{"accessibilityCaption":"Help us reach our $2,000,000 goal","conditional":[{"conditions":[{"maxColumns":4,"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"hidden":false}],"hidden":true,"identifier":"_anf-figure-4","imageIdentifier":"a3b4c00edd84caae3f485ac41e12c728","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"figure","type":"scalable_image"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-31","layout":"ComponentLayout-16","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-3","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-37","layout":"ComponentLayout-253","role":"body","text":"At this unsettling time","textStyle":"_anf-cts-7","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-28","layout":"ComponentLayout-248","role":"container","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-1","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":403,"start":1788},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-47"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-16","role":"body","text":"We hope you appreciated this article. Before you close this tab, we want to ask if you could spare 37 seconds to support our most important fundraising appeal of the year.\n\nWhen democratic norms and political stability erode, the role of journalism as an engine of scrutiny, truth and accountability becomes increasingly important.\n\nAt the Guardian, we see it as our job not only to report the facts as we find them, but to provide the historical and global context necessary to fully understand the turbulent times in which we’re living. Humanity, curiosity and honesty guide us, and our work is rooted in solidarity with ordinary people and hope for our shared future. We don’t have a single viewpoint, but we do have a shared set of values. We proudly platform voices of dissent, and we are fearless when it comes to investigating corruption and challenging power.\n\nNot every news organization sees its mission this way – and nor is their editorial independence as ironclad as ours. In the past year, several large media outlets have caved to outside pressure at the behest of their corporate and billionaire owners. We are thankful the Guardian is different. \n\nOur only financial obligation is to fund independent journalism in perpetuity: we have no ultrarich owner, no shareholders, no corporate bosses with the power to overrule or influence our editorial decisions. Reader support is what guarantees our survival and safeguards our independence – and every cent we receive is reinvested in our work. \n\nIt has never been more urgent, or more perilous, to pursue reporting that holds power to account and counters the spread of misinformation – and at the Guardian we make our journalism free and accessible to all. Can you spare just 37 seconds now to support our year-end appeal?  We value whatever you can spare, but a recurring contribution makes the most impact, enabling greater investment in our most crucial, fearless journalism. As our thanks to you, we can offer you some great benefits – including unlimited access to the premium Guardian news app and far fewer fundraising messages on our site. We've made it very quick to set up, so we hope you’ll consider it. Thank you. ","textStyle":"_anf-cts-6","type":"text"},{"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-2","layout":"ComponentLayout-259","role":"body","text":"Best value","textStyle":"_anf-cts-8","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-36","layout":"ComponentLayout-258","role":"container","style":"_anf-cs-5","type":"container"},{"components":[{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-3","layout":"ComponentLayout-153","role":"body","text":"Support $15/month","textStyle":"_anf-cts-9","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-38","layout":"ComponentLayout-152","role":"container","type":"container"},{"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-4","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":18,"start":7},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-48"}],"layout":"ComponentLayout-103","role":"body","text":"Unlock All-access digital benefits:","textStyle":"_anf-cts-10","type":"text"},{"components":[{"components":[{"components":[{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"dark"}],"hidden":true}],"identifier":"_anf-logo-4","imageIdentifier":"6af19638ce4a233280bce0b325914a2d","layout":"ComponentLayout-101","role":"logo","type":"image"},{"conditional":[{"conditions":[{"minSpecVersion":"1.10","preferredColorScheme":"light"}],"hidden":true}],"identifier":"_anf-logo-5","imageIdentifier":"8d575d30fdb20a3b22b853b83e9fc642","layout":"ComponentLayout-101","role":"logo","type":"image"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-50","layout":"ComponentLayout-100","role":"container","type":"container"},{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-body-5","layout":"ComponentLayout-104","role":"body","text":"Unlimited access to the Guardian app","textStyle